<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian s/adj Dec employment rises 4,500.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian s/adj Dec employment rises 4,500.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia's seasonally-adjusted estimate of the number of employed persons rose 4,500 in December to 8.40 million, against 8.40 million in November and 8.34 million a year earlier, the Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>The seasonally adjusted unemployment rate rise to 8.6 percent in December from 8.5 percent in November, compared with 8.1 percent in December 1995.</p>
<p>Economists had on average expected employment to rise around 5,000 in December, seasonally-adjusted, with the unemployment rate rising to 8.7 percent.  </p>
<p>AUSTRALIAN UNEMPLOYMENT</p>
<p>    (Seasonally adj)	 Dec 96	Nov 96	Dec 95</p>
<p>    Unemployment Rate     8.6 pct     8.5 pct	8.1 pct</p>
<p>    Employed		  8.40 mln    8.40 mln     8.34 mln</p>
<p>    Unemployed		794,500     775,200	738,300</p>
<p>    Participation Rate   63.6 pct    63.5 pct     63.8 pct</p>
<p>(Unadjusted)</p>
<p>    Unemployment Rate     8.7 pct     8.1 pct	8.2 pct</p>
<p>    Employed		  8.50 mln    8.39 mln     8.43 mln</p>
<p>    Unemployed		805,700     737,200	748,600</p>
<p>    Participation Rate   64.3 pct    63.2 pct     64.5 pct</p>
<p>(Trend Estimates)</p>
<p>    Unemployment Rate    8.7 pct	8.7 pct	8.4 pct</p>
<p>    Employed		 8.40 mln     8.39 mln     8.31 mln</p>
<p>    Unemployed	     796,100	796,100	765,400</p>
<p>    Participation Rate  63.6 pct     63.6 pct     63.8 pct</p>
<p>The Bureau said part-time employment rose around 3,700 in December, while full-time employment rose around 700.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
